-- Regression fixture: an ill-typed module auto-discovered via a RELATIVE
-- MARCH_LIB_PATH directory.  When the entry (libpath_entry.march) does NOT
-- reference it, reachability pruning drops it and the build succeeds; when the
-- entry DOES reference it (libpath_entry_ref.march), it stays in the build and
-- its type error must surface (exit 1).  The referenced-and-relative case also
-- guards the user_files path-canonicalization fix: spans carry the as-parsed
-- (relative) path, which must be recognised as user code so the diagnostic is
-- not misclassified as stdlib-internal and silently tolerated.
mod LibpathIllTyped do

  fn broken() : Int do
    -- type error: Int + String
    1 + "not an int"
  end

end
